course: dictionary
lesson: 12237
title: A batch sent together
level: primary-6
stars: 0
explain: A consignment is a batch of goods that is sent or delivered together, in one load. Look for clues like «a new consignment», «a consignment of» and words such as arrived, shipped or delivered. «The shop got a new consignment of phone cases today.» The word tells you the phone cases came together as one group, not one at a time.
explain: «The lorry carried a consignment of 400 boxes to the port.» Ask: what word would fit here? The number 400 and the word boxes are your clues. Swap in the load of 400 boxes and the sentence still makes sense, so a consignment is the whole load.
explain: The word also has a formal meaning: the act of handing something over to someone to look after or sell. «On consignment» is a shop phrase. «The artist left her paintings on consignment at the gallery.» The paintings stay in the gallery, and the artist is paid only when each one is sold.
fact: A consignment is a batch of goods sent or delivered together.
fact: «A consignment of 400 boxes» means 400 boxes sent as one load.
fact: The formal meaning is the act of handing something over to someone to look after or sell.
fact: «On consignment» means goods are left in a shop to sell, and the owner is paid only when they are sold.
fact: Clue words for a consignment are new, of, arrived, shipped and delivered.
exercise: «The shop got a new consignment of phone cases today.» What is a consignment here? | An empty box with no label | A single phone case | *A batch of goods delivered together | A type of shop
exercise: «The lorry carried a consignment of 400 boxes to the port.» How many boxes were in the consignment? | 4 | *400 | 4,000 | 40
exercise: The artist left her paintings «on consignment» at the gallery. When will she be paid? | When the gallery closes for the holidays | As soon as the paintings arrive at the gallery | *Only when each painting is sold | Before she has painted them
test: Ravi says a consignment is just one box. Is he right? | No, a consignment is a load of goods sent together | *No, it is a load of goods, so it can be many boxes | Yes, one box is always a consignment | Only if the box is very big
test: «The factory sent a consignment of shoes to every shop in town.» What was sent? | Shoes that were worn out | One pair of shoes for the manager | *A batch of shoes sent together | A lost parcel with no label
exam: Which meaning fits «the consignment of the old letters to the library, to be kept safe»? | A letter written by the librarian | *The act of handing the letters over to someone to look after | A load of letters sent by post in one batch | A shop that sells old letters
